From 92a9661b4dcee55ff99776836f31d9212f5b1942 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:33:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: store wake_check verbatim, refuse a probe
 redaction would change; redactor keeps idempotency_key and other identifier
 *_key values
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A park's wake_check went through the display redactor before it was stored
(tools/kanban_tools_park_args.py), and the lowercase assignment rule masked
idempotency_key='review:pr1305:<sha>' to 'review...26b2'. PR #1305's owner
parked on that probe; it could never match, and the card waited for its
fallback wake although both conditions held (t_01a1cf477dece56b).

- wake_check (kanban_block / kanban_schedule / kanban_continue) is stored
  byte-identical. A probe the redactor would change is refused with
  wake_check_secret, before the dry run executes it; the error names the
  assignment (or the word before a bare token) and says to read the secret
  from env or a file. human_request.resolved_check already refuses the same
  way (kanban_human_request._refuse_secret).
- agent/redact.py: exact identifier names idempotency_key, cache_key,
  sort_key, primary_key, partition_key, dedupe_key, dedup_key (any case)
  are never masked by the assignment passes (agent/redact_identifier_keys.py).
  Credential names (api_key, secret_key, private_key, access_key,
  AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, password, token) still mask.
- Comment redaction is unchanged; with the allowlist idempotency_key='…'
  survives in comments.

Proof: tests/agent/test_redact_identifier_key_names.py and
tests/tools/test_kanban_probe_verbatim.py: 20 failed / 9 passed on the parent
(d29b70bd0f), all pass here; the 92 test files that import agent.redact or
drive the park handlers pass (4197 passed, 6 skipped).
